@startuml
title ioScope Scenario View - Start FTDI Session with Tee-to-File
autonumber

actor User
participant ioQtScopeWindow as Window
participant ioOscilloscopeController as Controller
participant ioOscilloscopeModel as Model
participant ioLiveOscilloscopeSession as LiveSession
participant ioTappedReadableByteStream as Tapped
participant ioFtdiByteStream as FtdiIn
participant ioFileByteStream as FileOut
participant ioPipelineController as PipelineController
participant ioDetailedOscilloscopeView as Detailed

User -> Window : click Start
Window -> Controller : start()
Controller -> Model : refreshSamples()
Controller -> Controller : _start_live_session()
Controller -> LiveSession : start(control_state)
LiveSession -> LiveSession : build input stream from FTDI settings
LiveSession -> FtdiIn : create(device_index=0)
LiveSession -> Tapped : wrap(FtdiIn, sample_history)
LiveSession -> LiveSession : build output stream from tee settings
LiveSession -> FileOut : create("demo_ftdi_capture.bin")
LiveSession -> LiveSession : build ioPipelineConfig
LiveSession -> PipelineController : create(cfg, Tapped, FileOut)
LiveSession -> PipelineController : start()
PipelineController -> PipelineController : writer.start()
PipelineController -> PipelineController : reader.start()
Controller -> Model : appendEvent("session_start")
Controller -> Detailed : render(ioRenderState)
Detailed --> User : detailed UI shows FTDI + tee=file status

note over LiveSession, PipelineController
The live session owns pipeline construction for the GUI mode.
The same backend transfer architecture is reused instead of
moving FTDI logic into the Qt layer.
end note
@enduml
